Darken the menu stripe of a lightened popup menu

The darken value of the menu stripe takes a shade of the popup menu
background. The style takes the plain shade while the option for a
lighter popup menu holds a value other than zero. That value is the
shipped default. The stripe colour then equals the background of the
menu, and a flat stripe appearance paints no stripe at all.

The stripe now takes the darker shade for every value of the lighter
popup menu. A flat stripe stands against the menu again. A popup menu
with no lightening keeps the colour of before, and the other stripe
colours do not move.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 13 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/common.h b/qt6/common/common.h
index b8545972..b1285a30 100644
--- a/qt6/common/common.h
+++ b/qt6/common/common.h
@@ -109,7 +109,10 @@ enum {
 
 #define FRAME_DARK_SHADOW 2
 #define FOCUS_SHADE(SEL)         (FOCUS_GLOW==opts.focus ? GLOW_MO : ((SEL) ? 3 : ORIGINAL_SHADE))
-#define MENU_STRIPE_SHADE (opts.lighterPopupMenuBgnd ? ORIGINAL_SHADE : 2)
+// The shade of the menu background that the darken stripe takes.
+#define MENU_STRIPE_DARK_SHADE 2
+#define MENU_STRIPE_SHADE (opts.lighterPopupMenuBgnd ? ORIGINAL_SHADE : \
+                           MENU_STRIPE_DARK_SHADE)
 #define MENU_SEP_SHADE    (opts.lighterPopupMenuBgnd ? 4 : 3)
 
 #define BGND_STRIPE_SHADE 0.95
diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
index 60d54c10..63d34cc2 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
@@ -4206,7 +4206,7 @@ QColor Style::menuStripeCol() const
     case SHADE_SELECTED:
         return m_highlightCols[MENU_STRIPE_SHADE];
     case SHADE_DARKEN:
-        return popupMenuCols()[MENU_STRIPE_SHADE];
+        return popupMenuCols()[MENU_STRIPE_DARK_SHADE];
     }
 }
 
